    pr_ref:  # fdb1
    description: "From dogfood round 2026-04-24 on `dev` @ f7b3f3f87. Surfaced while inspecting the Plan C `external_potential` bucket for whether it inherits WI-fozoh / WI-diruj mis-classification (it doesn't — but this separate gap does).\n\n## Symptom\n\nEvery Python direct dependency declared in `pyproject.toml` is classified as `supply_chain.tier=3` (external_dep) in the behaviour map, when it should be tier-2 (direct dependency).\n\nOn hypergumbo self-analysis, at least 38 distinct `external_potential` dsts correspond to known direct deps:\n\n- `click`, `rich`, `ruamel.yaml`, `pydantic`, `starlette`, `textual`, `textual.widgets`, `textual.containers`\n- `sentence_transformers`, `huggingface_hub`, `tree_sitter`, `hypothesis`\n- `pytest`, `bcrypt`, `proquint`, `protobuf`, `google.protobuf`\n- … plus ~20 others from transitive `pyproject.toml` declarations\n\nBecause all 525 distinct Python external dsts are tier-3, tier filtering in sketch / slice / supply-chain queries cannot distinguish \"this repo's own pinned dependency\" from \"some deep transitive stdlib thing.\" On polyglot repos that emphasize tier-2 in their dead-code / taint analysis, Python dependencies are systematically under-represented at the useful tier.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/ir.py` lines 700-712 in `create_boundary_nodes`:\n\n```python\n# Consult dependency manifest for Go/Java/Kotlin boundary nodes\nif dependency_manifest is not None and language in (\"go\", \"java\", \"kotlin\") and len(parts) >= 3:\n    import_path = parts[1]\n    manifest_tier = dependency_manifest.classify_import(import_path)\n    tier = manifest_tier.value\n    if tier == 2:\n        reason = (\n            \"direct dependency (go.mod)\" if language == \"go\"\n            else \"direct dependency (build manifest)\"\n        )\n```\n\nPython is absent from the language allow-list. So the tier always falls back to the default `tier = 3` set at line 698. The rest of the pipeline is wired — `DependencyManifest.classify_import` (supply_chain.py:70) is language-agnostic at the interface level; what's missing is the equivalent of `jvm_deps.py` for pyproject.toml.\n\n## Parallel prior work\n\nThe JVM side shipped in v2.7.0:\n- `packages/hypergumbo-lang-mainstream/src/hypergumbo_lang_mainstream/jvm_deps.py` parses `build.gradle` / `build.gradle.kts` / `pom.xml` into `DependencyManifest`.\n- `supply_chain.py` consumes the manifest; `create_boundary_nodes` is wired for java / kotlin.\n- `go.py:423` does the equivalent for `go.mod`.\n\nA `py_deps.py` would follow the same pattern: parse `pyproject.toml` (and optionally `setup.py`, `requirements*.txt`) to produce a `DependencyManifest` of direct deps.\n\n## Fix sketch\n\n1. New module `packages/hypergumbo-lang-mainstream/src/hypergumbo_lang_mainstream/py_deps.py` with a `parse_pyproject(root_path) -> DependencyManifest` parallel to `jvm_deps.py:parse_manifest`. Handles `[project].dependencies` (PEP 621), `[project.optional-dependencies]` (extras, tier-2), and `[tool.poetry.dependencies]` (Poetry convention). Distribution-name-to-import-name resolution via `importlib.metadata.packages_distributions()` (e.g. `ruamel.yaml` → `ruamel.yaml`, `PyYAML` → `yaml`).\n2. Wire into `cli.py` alongside `jvm_deps` — load the manifest during profile, pass to `create_boundary_nodes`.\n3. Extend `ir.py:702` allow-list: `language in (\"go\", \"java\", \"kotlin\", \"python\")`.\n4. Extend the `reason` string formatting: `\"direct dependency (pyproject.toml)\"` for python.\n\n## Scope expansion / invariants\n\n- JavaScript / TypeScript have `package.json` but no manifest-aware tiering either. Likely has the same bug, but let's confirm on a diverse JS repo before filing. (Separately tracked as follow-up if found.)\n- Ruby (`Gemfile`), PHP (`composer.json`), Rust (`Cargo.toml`), Elixir (`mix.exs`) — all equivalent gaps. The language list in `ir.py:702` is the single sentinel for which languages got manifest-aware tiering; anything missing from that list defaults to tier-3.\n- Invariant candidate: \"For every supported language with a canonical package manifest, `ir.py:702` must consult that manifest for tier-2 classification of direct deps.\" Currently held only for go / java / kotlin.\n\n## Validation\n\nExpected bakeoff signal on a Python-heavy repo: tier-2 node count jumps from ~0 to (# of pyproject direct deps), tier-3 drops correspondingly. Sketch output should start ranking symbols from `click` / `rich` / etc. differently (centrality penalty for tier-3 no longer blanket-applies to direct deps). File as `awaits_bakeoff_validation` at merge time."  # fdb1
    fields: {}  # fdb1
- op: discuss  # 719d
